{# DEPARTMENTS · CONFIGURE — how this section behaves, who may change it, and
   the vocabulary it writes with.

   READ-ONLY, AND THAT IS THE DESIGN. Every line here is a fact about the model
   or about who may do what: the two scopes, the unique-name rule, which
   permission each act asks for. A control that let one of them be changed
   would be a second place the rule lived. The one list that IS editable has
   its own section, and this page hands over to it rather than inlining it.

   THE STRIP ABOVE IS THIS SURFACE'S SECTIONS, written by the shell's frame
   from the sections contract — the same one position a data tab's strip
   occupies. #}
{% extends '@Shell/page.html.twig' %}
{% import '@Team/positions/_bits.html.twig' as pm %}
{% import '@Team/departments/_bits.html.twig' as di %}

{% block title %}Departments{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {{ include('@Team/_stylesheets.html.twig') }}
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}
    <a href="{{ path('team_departments_overview') }}">uhifadhi</a> / departments / configure
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}Departments{% endblock %}
{% block shell_page_subtitle %}How this section behaves, who may change it, and the vocabulary it writes with.{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page %}
    <div data-dp>
        {# ADDING A DEPARTMENT — here, and only here (owner 2026-09-22): the
           register shows what exists; creation is configuration. #}
        {% set hasAreas = areas|length > 0 %}
        {# CREATE — the scope question first (area-first by default, the narrow
           correctable choice), then the name, and for an area, which one. #}
        <form class="crcard" method="post" action="{{ path('team_department_create') }}"
              data-controller="uhifadhi--team-bundle--department"
              data-scope="{{ hasAreas ? 'area' : 'org' }}"
              data-create-department
              data-uhifadhi--team-bundle--department-hint-area-value="<b>Just an area.</b> This department will belong only to the area you pick above and will not appear in the others &mdash; the safer default, and easy to widen later."
              data-uhifadhi--team-bundle--department-hint-org-value="<b>Org-wide.</b> This department will belong to the organization and appear in every area as an inherited department.">
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="scope" value="{{ hasAreas ? 'area' : 'org' }}"
                   data-uhifadhi--team-bundle--department-target="scopeField">
            <div class="crgrid">
                <div class="crfield">
                    <span class="crlab">Scope &mdash; just this area, or org-wide?</span>
                    <div class="seg" role="tablist">
                        <button type="button" class="{{ hasAreas ? 'on' : '' }}" data-scope-set="area"
                                {{ hasAreas ? '' : 'disabled' }}
                                data-uhifadhi--team-bundle--department-target="segment"
                                data-action="uhifadhi--team-bundle--department#setScope">{{ di.icon_area() }} Just an area</button>
                        <button type="button" class="{{ hasAreas ? '' : 'on' }}" data-scope-set="org"
                                data-uhifadhi--team-bundle--department-target="segment"
                                data-action="uhifadhi--team-bundle--department#setScope">{{ di.icon_org() }} Org-wide</button>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="crfield crpick">
                    <span class="crlab">Which area?</span>
                    <select name="area" aria-label="Area">
                        {% for area in areas %}
                            <option value="{{ area.uuidString }}">{{ area.name }}</option>
                        {% else %}
                            <option value="">No areas yet</option>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </select>
                </div>
                <div class="crfield grow">
                    <span class="crlab">Name</span>
                    <input type="text" class="fld" name="name" placeholder="New department"
                           aria-label="New department name" required>
                </div>
                <button class="cta" type="submit">{{ pm.icon_plus() }} Add department</button>
            </div>
            <div class="crhint">
                {{ pm.icon_info() }}
                <span data-uhifadhi--team-bundle--department-target="hint">
                    {% if hasAreas %}
                        <b>Just an area.</b> This department will belong only to the area you pick above and will not
                        appear in the others &mdash; the safer default, and easy to widen later.
                    {% else %}
                        <b>Org-wide.</b> There are no areas yet, so a department can only be organization-wide for now.
                        It will belong to the organization and appear in every area.
                    {% endif %}
                </span>
            </div>
        </form>


        <div class="grid g2">
            <div class="c">
                <span class="tab">The register<span class="src">&middot; how it reads</span></span>
                <div class="rln"><span>Tab on open</span><span class="mono d">Overview</span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span>Group order</span><span class="mono d">org-wide, then each area by name</span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span>Row order inside a group</span><span class="mono d">by name</span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span>A deactivated department</span><span class="mono d">stays in the register, greyed, with a Reactivate action</span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span>Departments now</span><span class="mono d">{{ departments }} active</span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="c">
                <span class="tab">Creating a department<span class="src">&middot; the rules</span></span>
                <div class="rln"><span>Who may create one</span><span class="mono d"><span class="mono">team.manage</span></span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span>Name</span><span class="mono d">unique inside its scope, not across the installation</span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span>Scope chosen at creation</span><span class="mono d">yes &mdash; just an area, or org-wide</span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span>Default scope in the form</span><span class="mono d">just an area, where the installation has one</span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span>Changing scope later</span><span class="mono d">allowed &middot; a reason is required and recorded</span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span>Deleting a department</span><span class="mono d">never &mdash; it is deactivated, and keeps its history</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid g2">
            <div class="c">
                <span class="tab">Access<span class="src">&middot; permissions</span></span>
                <div class="rln"><span>Who can see Departments</span><span class="mono d"><span class="mono">team.manage</span></span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span>Who can create and rename</span><span class="mono d"><span class="mono">team.manage</span></span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span>Who can change a scope</span><span class="mono d"><span class="mono">team.manage</span> &middot; a reason is stored with it</span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span>Who can attach a module</span><span class="mono d"><span class="mono">team.manage</span></span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span>Reach</span><span class="mono d">an area-level department confines its holders&rsquo; authority to that area</span></div>
                <p class="use">Each tab is its own route, so access is enforced per page.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="c">
                <span class="tab">Positions &amp; people<span class="src">&middot; Team</span></span>
                <div class="sxlead">
                    <span class="t">{{ ux_icon('shell:users', {width: 15, height: 15}) }}<span><b>Read-only here.</b> A department&rsquo;s positions and its people belong to Team; this section neither creates nor edits them.</span></span>
                    <span class="a"><a class="cta" href="{{ path('team_positions') }}">Open Team</a></span>
                </div>
                <div class="rln"><span>Where positions are edited</span><span class="mono d">Team &middot; Positions</span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span>Where people are assigned</span><span class="mono d">Team &middot; People</span></div>
                <div class="rln"><span>What Departments holds</span><span class="mono d">the department itself, its scope, its kind and what it attaches</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="c">
            <span class="tab">Lists<span class="src">&middot; its own section</span></span>
            <div class="sxlead">
                <span class="t">{{ ux_icon('shell:settings', {width: 15, height: 15}) }}<span><b>The vocabulary this section writes with.</b> The two scopes are the model and are not a list; the kinds are, and an organization wanting one more adds it there rather than in code.</span></span>
                <span class="a"><a class="cta" href="{{ path('team_departments_configure_lists') }}">Open Lists</a></span>
            </div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Department kinds</span><span class="mono d">{{ kinds|length }} &middot; editable</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Scopes</span><span class="mono d">{{ scopes|map(s => s.value)|join(' &middot; ')|raw }} &mdash; fixed, two, not editable</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Goal kinds</span><span class="mono d">module-contributed &middot; they arrive with the module that can measure them</span></div>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
